    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "The config spread order (`{ module: { … }, ...swc }`) allows callers to accidentally override the interop settings you’re trying to enforce (e.g. by passing `swc.module` with a different `noInterop`/`type`). If the intent is to guarantee CJS interop, merge `swc` first and then override/merge `module` so `noInterop: false` can’t be lost (ideally with a deep merge for `module`).\n```suggestion\n        ...swc,\n        module: {\n          ...(swc.module || {}),\n          type: 'commonjs',\n          noInterop: false,\n        },\n```",
    "commit_id": "671ad53678710b8b8d3f6a7bcf91b8f62b2fb8ea",
    "created_at": "2026-03-04T14:44:27Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -129,7 +129,13 @@ export function createCJSConfig({\n       createResolvePlugin(),\n       createCommonjsPlugin(),\n       ...preSwcPlugins,\n-      createSwcPlugin(swc),\n+      createSwcPlugin({\n+        module: {\n+          type: 'commonjs',\n+          noInterop: false,\n+        },\n+        ...swc,",
