    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Setting SWC `module.type: 'commonjs'` in `createCJSConfig` will transform source `import`/`export` into `require`/`exports` before Rollup analyzes the module graph. Because `createCommonjsPlugin()` is configured to only include `node_modules` (not local `src` files), Rollup may no longer be able to discover and include internal dependencies for packages that use a single entry (e.g. `packages/react-instantsearch-nextjs` / `react-instantsearch-router-nextjs`), which can lead to incomplete/incorrect CJS builds. Prefer keeping SWC module output as ESM and configure CJS default-export interop at the Rollup output level (e.g. `output.interop`), or otherwise ensure local sources are handled by the CommonJS plugin if SWC is going to emit CJS.",
    "commit_id": "671ad53678710b8b8d3f6a7bcf91b8f62b2fb8ea",
    "created_at": "2026-03-04T14:44:28Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -129,7 +129,13 @@ export function createCJSConfig({\n       createResolvePlugin(),\n       createCommonjsPlugin(),\n       ...preSwcPlugins,\n-      createSwcPlugin(swc),\n+      createSwcPlugin({\n+        module: {\n+          type: 'commonjs',\n+          noInterop: false,\n+        },\n+        ...swc,\n+      }),",
